    doubled_params = dict(shipping)
    doubled_params["n"] *= 2
    start = time.perf_counter()
    doubled = make_instance(seed=77, **doubled_params)

codex
The triage now points to rejection, not a build. The theorem-backed promise is solved by the proof itself: Lemma 2 constructs the six-gadget partition by constant-size local updates, and the proof of Theorem 2 colors those pieces by another local propagation pass. I’m quantifying that at the largest hand-writable representative and checking whether Track B has any real compression gap before recording the decision.
