I found a viable honest route: Track B, native graph objects, no reduction. I’ll use cubic graphs built from a hidden vertex-disjoint \(C_4\)-factor plus a random external perfect matching, rejecting matchings that create extra 4-cycles. Each planted square composes an exact two-color coupon certificate, while the plant is not exposed in the rendered instance. The reference solver independently enumerates the unique 4-cycles in linear time for cubic graphs; cheap label, greedy, BFS, and randomized no-tool heuristics must all fail.
