- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1512.04748/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1512.04748/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.04748) supplies a constructive algorithm, so Track A would be false. The generator instead inverse-constructs cubic graphs around hidden \(C_4\)-factor colourings and honestly declares Track B.

Local results:

- G1–G9 all pass.
- Random guessing: 0/200,000.
- Seven attacks, including randomized greedy and spectral: 0/8 each.
- Reference square-factor algorithm: 8/8, 7,056 operations.
- Answer: 449 characters, 224 atoms.
- Intended route: 280 operations.

The result is not yet shippable: all three oracle arms were rejected before inference with OpenRouter HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.” The repository validator confirms the hardening transcript is the sole blocker. No `REJECTED.md` was written because this is an external-service failure, not a failure of G, H, or V.
